    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>That's a pretty intense way to put it. So you're saying that the decline in aesthetic quality is basically a good thing because it's more \"morally urgent\"? It feels like you're dismissing the idea that art should actually be good to look at or skillfully made. Aren't we losing something fundamental if we just treat art as a political pamphlet?",
